ADD THESE STYLES (REQUIRED)

📍 Put this in your main CSS file or inside <style>

/* INITIAL STATE */
.info-card {
  opacity: 0;
  transform: translateY(32px) scale(0.98);
  transition:
    opacity 0.6s ease,
    transform 0.6s cubic-bezier(.22,.61,.36,1);
  will-change: transform, opacity;
}

/* ACTIVE (WHEN IN VIEW) */
.info-card.is-visible {
  opacity: 1;
  transform: translateY(0) scale(1);
}

/* OPTIONAL: subtle icon pop */
.info-card.is-visible .bullet {
  animation: bulletPop 0.5s ease forwards;
}

@keyframes bulletPop {
  from { transform: scale(0.6); opacity: 0; }
  to   { transform: scale(1); opacity: 1; }
}


This gives you:

smooth vertical rise

slight scale-in (premium feel)

GPU-friendly animation

2️⃣ ADD THIS JAVASCRIPT (NO LIBRARIES)

📍 Put this at the bottom of index.html, after the card exists in the DOM:

<script>
  const infoCards = document.querySelectorAll('.info-card');

  const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
    entries => {
      entries.forEach(entry => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add('is-visible');
        } else {
          // 🔥 remove class so animation replays every time
          entry.target.classList.remove('is-visible');
        }
      });
    },
    {
      threshold: 0.35
    }
  );

  infoCards.forEach(card => observer.observe(card));
</script>

3️⃣ NOTHING ELSE TO CHANGE

Your HTML stays exactly as-is:

<article class="info-card" aria-labelledby="card-title" role="region">